invariant: INV-58
file: p256_sign.c
catches: p256_sign_test
reason: sign_hedged hands sign_digest no noise, so the hedged entry signs
  with the RFC 6979 nonce. Two signatures over one message are the same
  bytes again, which is the shape a differential fault attack wants. Each
  signature still verifies. bin/p256_sign_test requires the hedged
  vectors' bytes and requires them to differ from the RFC 6979 bytes.

--- old
    return sign_digest(widemul, cpu, priv, msg_hash, noise, sig, cap, sig_len);
--- new
    return sign_digest(widemul, cpu, priv, msg_hash, NULL, sig, cap, sig_len);
